---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const pageTitle = "About Erik Rutledge | Rutledge Digital";
const pageDescription = "Get to know Erik Rutledge, the person behind Rutledge Digital, and learn about his approach to building better websites for small businesses.";
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <section class="hero section-wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> THE PERSON BEHIND RUTLEDGE DIGITAL</p>
      <h1>Hey, I’m Erik.<br /><span class="accent">I make the web work for you.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">I’m the founder of Rutledge Digital. I work with businesses to turn ideas, challenges, and big plans into useful, thoughtful websites. I am passionate about small business, local community, and helping people who dedicate themselves to providing a service or product to others.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/contact/">Let’s work together <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="#my-approach">How I work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-proof"><span>Owner & developer</span><span>Based in Utah</span><span>Eager to help your business</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art" aria-label="Portrait of Erik Rutledge">
      <img src="/public/me-transparent.png" alt="Portrait of Erik Rutledge" width="100%" height="350" />
      <span class="art-label label-top">ERIK RUTLEDGE</span>
      <span class="art-label label-bottom">FOUNDER · RUTLEDGE DIGITAL</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro-band">
    <div class="section-wrap intro-grid">
      <p class="eyebrow">A QUICK INTRODUCTION</p>
      <p class="intro-statement">Good work starts with understanding people. <span>Before I think about pages, features, or code, I want to understand the person behind the business and what they’re trying to accomplish.</span></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-wrap section-block">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">MY STORY</p><h2>How I got<br />to doing this.</h2></div>
      <p class="note-panel">I have always been passionate about building and creating. I loved woodshop class, ceramics, painting, and working with my hands. I started my higher education majoring in mechanical engineering and was mostly done when the world shut down in the COVID-19 pandemic. I pivoted into something that could be done from anywhere when everything went remote: software engineering. It satisfied that urge I have for creation, creativity, and problem solving. I started doing freelance projects for friends my senior year and graduated with a bachelor's degree in software engineering December 2024. I guess I was doing an okay job because when one project would end I would be referred to someone else that needed website help. Pretty soon I had a pool of clients and a wide array of tools under my belt. I had planned to use this work to pad my resume, apply for jobs, and move onto the next thing, but found myself enjoying the people and interactions too much. I created Rutledge Digital LLC as a way to officially dedicate my efforts towards helping small businesses and the people that operate them. I love learning and each project allows me a glimpse into a different industry I would have never been exposed to otherwise. Whether it's a pop-up market that sells custom trucker hats, a manufacturer and distributor of wheels for supercars, a studio rental business for photoshoots, a holistic medicine and integrative phsychiatry professional, and so on. What I love is getting to know the people, their passions, their problems, and making myself as valuable to them as I can be. I'm continually drawn back because I want to know what the next business is and how I can help them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="note-panel">
      <p class="eyebrow">WORDS I LIVE BY</p>
      <h2>“You don't have to do everything yourself, focus on what fulfills you and get good at it then allow others to help you with the things they love to do.”</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro-band" id="my-approach">
    <div class="section-wrap section-block">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">MY APPROACH</p><h2>What you can<br />expect from me.</h2></div>
      </div>
      <div class="service-grid">
        <article class="service-card"><span class="service-index">01 / LISTEN</span><div class="service-icon">◎</div><h3>Understand first</h3><p>I like to learn about a your business, audience, priorities, and challenges recommending a solution and making a plan.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><span class="service-index">02 / BUILD</span><div class="service-icon">↗</div><h3>Targeted implementation</h3><p>I want to meet you where you are, we don't have to tear everything down or start over. If you have a website that is mostly good, we can target the parts that will make it exceptional.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><span class="service-index">03 / SUPPORT</span><div class="service-icon">⟳</div><h3>Stay in your corner</h3><p>I want celebrate each business success alongside you and help whenever it is needed. You decide if you want occasional communication, a project handoff with instruction, or ongoing support. </p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-wrap section-block">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">OUTSIDE THE SCREEN</p><h2>A few things that make me, <span class="accent">me.</span></h2></div>
    </div>
    <div class="service-grid">
      <article class="service-card"><span class="service-index">01 / WHEN I’M NOT CODING</span><div class="service-icon">↗</div><h3>Woodworking</h3><p>The itch to work with my hands isn't completely scratched at a computer all day. I love working with wood and creating beautiful pieces.</p></article>
      <article class="service-card"><span class="service-index">02 / CURRENTLY INTO</span><div class="service-icon">◈</div><h3>Watercolor painting</h3><p>I have a travel-sized watercolor kit I take with me on adventures and it really allows me to enjoy the places I go, then at the end you have a physical memory of that moment.</p></article>
      <article class="service-card"><span class="service-index">03 / A FUN FACT</span><div class="service-icon">◎</div><h3>Ambidextrous</h3><p>I guess it's technically called being cross dominant, but I'm not a righty or a leftie. Everything I learn makes me experiment which hand feels more natural. I throw with my left hand, but write with my right.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-wrap section-block">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">WHO I WORK BEST WITH</p><h2>Good people.<br /><span class="accent">Good problems to solve.</span></h2></div>
    </div>
    <div class="service-list">
      <div class="service-row"><span class="service-index">01</span><div><h2>E-Commerce brands with growing pains</h2><p>There's nothing wrong with SquareSpace, Wix, or Shopify sites, but the options can be limiting. Without technical knowledge it's hard to make your vision into reality using a website builder. I love creating custom themes, making plug-ins, and adding character to existing sites.</p></div></div>
      <div class="service-row"><span class="service-index">02</span><div><h2>Creating your first website</h2><p>Many of the businesses I work with start at pop-ups and markets, but at a certain point you reach the edge of that client pool. Brainstorming the best direction for a business looking to expand on the web is my bread and butter. </p></div></div>
      <div class="service-row"><span class="service-index">03</span><div><h2>Win-win scenarios</h2><p>Small businesses don't often have the budget to hire an agency to create and maintain their web presence. I want you to walk away with a weight off your back, like a problem that you couldn't figure out has been solved.</p></div></div>
    </div>
    <p>Don’t see yourself in this list? <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Tell me what you have in mind <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="section-wrap cta-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR TURN</p>
      <h2>Now you know me,<br /><span class="accent">tell me about your business.</span></h2>
      <p class="hero-lede cta-lede">Have a project in mind, a challenge to solve, or just a few questions? I’d be glad to hear from you.</p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/contact/">Let’s start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
